path the staged-change reader classifies and every claim or current copy it looks up is read from a lossless, unquoted record listing, so a path that would otherwise be quoted is judged like any other. At the commit-time hold, each listed change is compared with HEAD, which is the commit's parent only for an ordinary commit. An amend is therefore compared with the commit it replaces; a cherry-pick, revert, rebase, or non-conflicting merge commit is written without the commit-time check; and a hand fast-forward creates no commit. A commit in a linked worktree on the integration branch while the primary checkout is on another branch is read as elsewhere, so a non-close change is not judged and a later close compares against the edited copy. Each named residue is caught after the fact only by the merge-time mint, and only when its before revision predates the change.\""," rationale = \"The same changed checklist is consulted at dispatch, hand close, merge and adjudication. One digest and covering predicate keep readers from accepting different texts or treating a verdict about an earlier text as a release.\""," test_refs = \"TC-325, TC-326\""," status = \"Approved\""]},{"oldStart":3283,"oldLines":7,"newStart":3283,"newLines":7,"lines":[" title = \"Changed Done-when text is held at every build, close and merge transition\""," module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/agent_loop.py;project-trajectory/scripts/integrate.py\""," code_symbol = \"routed_session/build_hold;_done_when_refusal/staged_done_when_refusal\"","-detail = \"After routed_session selects a build or rework session, build_hold asks LLR-307's lane_hold and returns the worker's HELD human outcome when a blessing is owed; review sessions, critiques and adjudication rows are not held, and worker_endstate asks no hold. The merge refusal ladder asks the same predicate after its close records and refuses an unblessed changed closed checklist. The pre-commit done-when-blessed step invokes the staged-close arm, which r